    <GaugingStation location="Codford" name="Chitterne Brook" number="43028">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Crump weir with single concrete crest and brick walls and footbridge over structure. Previously station number 43801.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Bypassing is not significant, only at extremes. Weir seen to be drowned at 0.44m. One peak flow rating applied across the period of record.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Crump weir with single concrete crest and brick walls, 3.0m wide, with a footbridge over the structure.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2020 (WINFAP Files v9).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Subject to stream support as part of an EA/Water Company operating agreement.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">The catchment area consists of Upper Cretaceous (Upper and Middle Chalk), valley gravel and alluvium. No major urbanisation in the catchment. Land use rural and agricultural.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">R</Comment>
        </Comments>
